The SuperCollider parser uses the Spl Ast and Lexer.

At present the only difference in the Parser is the assignment syntax.

```
$ cd ~/sw/stsc3/Language/Smalltalk/
$ diff Spl/Parser.y SuperCollider/Parser.y
2c2
< module Language.Smalltalk.Spl.Parser where
---
> module Language.Smalltalk.SuperCollider.Parser where
116c116
<     : identifier ':=' expression { SplExprAssignment $1 $3 }
---
>     : identifier '=' expression { SplExprAssignment $1 $3 }
121c121
<     : primary '[' basic_expression ']' ':=' basic_expression { SplBasicExpression $1 (Just (splConstructDotMessage "at:put" [$3, $6])) }
---
>     : primary '[' basic_expression ']' '=' basic_expression { SplBasicExpression $1 (Just (splConstructDotMessage "at:put" [$3, $6])) }
$
```
